  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n\nThe approach leverages a mathematical transformation to linearize the non-convex overlap objective, enabling the use of efficient Linear Programming (LP) techniques. By recognizing that the overlap integral can be approximated as a linear combination of shifted h values, we reformulate the problem to minimize the maximum overlap across all shifts. This method avoids the pitfalls of gradient descent and PSO by directly addressing the problem's structure through a sequence of feasibility checks, making it computationally robust and efficient.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n\nVariables:\n- h \u2208 \u211d^{n_points}, h[i] \u2208 [0, 1], \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2\n- dx = 2.0 / n_points\n- C\u2085 is the minimal maximum overlap value we seek\n\nObjective:\nMinimize C\u2085 such that for all shifts k:\n  (h * (1 - h_k))_{overlap} \u2264 C\u2085\n\nWhere h_k is h shifted by k*dx, and the overlap integral is approximated by:\nC\u2085 \u2265 (h[i] * (1 - h[(i + k) % n_points])) * dx summed over valid i ranges\n\nConstraints:\n1. 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n2. \u2211h[i] * dx = 1 \u2192 \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n\na. Initialization:\n   - Set n_points = 200\n   - Initialize lower (C_low) and upper (C_high) bounds for binary search\n   - Set initial h based on initial_h_values if available, else uniform\n\nb. Binary Search Loop:\n   - While C_high - C_low > \u03b5 (tolerance) and time < budget:\n     - Compute mid = (C_low + C_high) / 2\n     - Formulate and solve feasibility LP for mid\n     - If feasible: update C_high = mid\n     - Else: update C_low = mid\n     - Track best feasible h\n\nc. LP Feasibility Check:\n   - For each shift k:\n     - Compute the shifted overlap constraints\n     - Ensure \u2211 h[i]*(1 - h[(i+k) % n_points]) * dx \u2264 mid\n   - Solve LP to find h satisfying constraints\n\nd. Post-Processing:\n   - Retrieve best h and compute exact C\u2085 using evaluator\n   - Ensure h satisfies constraints\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n\n- n_points = 200 balances precision and computation time\n- Binary search tolerance \u03b5 = 1e-4 for precision\n- Initial C bounds: [0, 0.5] scaled by dx considerations\n- Feasibility check uses LP relaxation for efficiency\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n\n- Time allocation: ~50 iterations of binary search, each LP solve in ~1-2s\n- Robustness: handles infeasibility by adjusting bounds and tracking best valid h\n- Early termination if time budget nears\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n\n- Validate h satisfies constraints\n- Recompute C\u2085 with evaluator for final score\n- Return (h_values, C\u2085, n_points) with best solution",
